WEBVTT

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:09.102
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Most people think that people who get up early do

00:00:09.103 --> 00:00:11.313
better in life and get more done.

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:19.618
Many very successful and super-productive people get up between 4 and 6 a.m.,

00:00:21.209 --> 00:00:28.075
for example: Tim Cook, Richard Branson, and Oprah Winfrey.

00:00:29.633 --> 00:00:33.168
However, not all successful people are larks.

00:00:33.973 --> 00:00:43.043
Famous night owls include Barack Obama, Charles Darwin, and Elvis Presley.

00:00:44.947 --> 00:00:48.045
It’s a good idea to match your job to your type,

00:00:48.538 --> 00:00:53.036
so owls are more suited to evening work or night shifts.

00:00:54.845 --> 00:00:57.045
Let’s look at some other factors.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.749
More women are larks.

00:01:00.362 --> 00:01:02.412
More men are owls.

00:01:03.622 --> 00:01:07.173
Teenagers of either sex are usually owls.

00:01:08.823 --> 00:01:11.191
Older people are usually larks.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:17.237
But actually, around 60% of people are a mix of the two types.

00:01:19.298 --> 00:01:21.698
Type is also linked to personality.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.773
Larks are normally more self-disciplined and orderly,

00:01:27.517 --> 00:01:30.433
but owls are more extrovert and open.

00:01:32.289 --> 00:01:34.500
So, the big question is…

00:01:34.881 --> 00:01:39.810
Who is happier: the larks or the owls?

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:45.941
Well, studies have shown that…larks are happier!

00:01:47.343 --> 00:01:52.607
Morning people are generally happier with life and have fewer mental health problems.

00:01:53.903 --> 00:01:56.183
Owls are more at risk of depression.

00:01:57.931 --> 00:02:01.109
But scientists think that it is possible to change your type.

00:02:03.131 --> 00:02:08.134
If you want to become a lark, you can stop using digital devices in the evening,

00:02:09.448 --> 00:02:13.884
practise going to bed earlier, and give yourself an early-morning reward,

00:02:15.091 --> 00:02:20.351
for example, a delicious cup of coffee or some time on your iPad.

00:02:22.148 --> 00:02:24.176
There’s good news for owls, though.

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:27.558
If you keep busy and motivated during the day,

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:30.777
it might be easier to go to sleep earlier at night.

00:02:32.649 --> 00:02:37.140
So the next day, you can fly out of bed, happy as a lark!